      "title": "Pressure swing: adsorb at high pressure, desorb at low",
      "description": "The drying tower works at line pressure (red); the desiccant adsorbs water vapour. The other tower is vented to atmosphere (blue) and swept by a small part of the dry air (purge, typically ~ 15–20 % for heatless dryers) which carries the water out through the silencer. Towers switch every few minutes. Typical pressure dew point −40 °C (−70 °C with molecular sieve).",
